{{also|tausend}}
==German==

===Etymology===
Nominalization of {{m|de|tausend}}. The interjection is short either for {{m|de||potz tausend Teufel}} (16th century) or for {{der|de|gmh|tûsentlisteler}}, later {{m|de|Tausendkünstler|t=the devil as a master of a thousand ruses, arts}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈtaʊ̯zənt/|[ˈtaʊ̯.zn̩t]}}
* {{audio|de|De-Tausend.ogg}}
* {{hyph|de|Tau|send}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n,s,-[see usage notes]:e:en}}

# [[thousand]] {{gloss|set or unit of one thousand items}}
#: {{uxi|de|ein halbes '''Tausend'''|half a '''thousand'''}}
#: {{ux|de|Nach dem ersten '''Tausend''' habe ich noch zwei weitere '''Tausend''' bestellt.|After the first '''thousand''' I ordered two more '''thousands'''.}} 
# {{lb|de|in the plural}} [[thousands]], [[a lot]] {{gloss|unspecified large quantity}}
#: {{ux|de|Es kamen '''Tausende''' Zuschauer / von Zuschauern.|t=There were '''thousands''' of spectators.}}
#: {{ux|de|Es kamen viele '''Tausend(e)''' Zuschauer / von Zuschauern.|t=There were many '''thousands''' spectators.}}
#: {{ux|de|Die '''Tausende(n)''' (von) Zuschauer(n) waren begeistert.|t=The '''thousands''' of spectators were ethusiastic.}}

====Usage notes====
* In sense 1, the plural is always unchanged. In sense 2, it can be unchanged optionally after an indefinite numeral such as {{m|de|[[viel]]e}} or {{m|de|[[etlich]]e}}. Otherwise the standard plural for sense 2 is {{m|de||Tausende}}. However, it is also fairly common to use adjectival declension in the plural, meaning that the form becomes {{m|de||Tausenden}} after articles and determiners, otherwise {{m|de||Tausende}}.
* A following noun may be added as an [[apposition]] or with {{m|de|von|t=of}}.

